    <item>
      <title>How to Deploy Rootless HAProxy as Podman Quadlet</title>
      <link>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-deploy-rootless-haproxy-as-podman-quadlet/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Sep 2024 16:24:34 +0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-deploy-rootless-haproxy-as-podman-quadlet/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;



&lt;img class=&#34;badge&#34;
	src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/Linux-FCC624?logo=linux&amp;logoColor=FFF&amp;style=flat&#34;
	alt=&#34;Linux Badge&#34; /&gt;





&lt;img class=&#34;badge&#34;
	src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/Podman-892CA0?logo=podman&amp;logoColor=FFF&amp;style=flat&#34;
	alt=&#34;Podman Badge&#34; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&#34;note&#34;&gt;This post is raw. No grammar is checked.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;When doing local development or just tinkering with this or that, quite often
you want to expose something to the Internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When it&amp;rsquo;s just single &amp;ldquo;something&amp;rdquo;, then you can just forward your port 80 from
router, to your machine&amp;rsquo;s &amp;ldquo;something&amp;rdquo; port.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But this falls appart if you have two &amp;ldquo;something&amp;rdquo; you want to expose to the
Internet. You can&amp;rsquo;t forward single &lt;code&gt;80&lt;/code&gt; port from your router to two different
applications running on your machine. Because one application will be running
for example on &lt;code&gt;8080&lt;/code&gt; port and the other on &lt;code&gt;8081&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How to Integrate Flyway Into Linux Desktop Environment</title>
      <link>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-integrate-flyway-into-linux-desktop-environment/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 05 Aug 2024 18:33:04 +0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-integrate-flyway-into-linux-desktop-environment/</guid>
      <description>&lt;img class=&#34;badge&#34;
	src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/Flyway-CC0200?logo=flyway&amp;logoColor=FFF&amp;style=flat&#34;
	alt=&#34;Flyway Badge&#34; /&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Today I decided to ditch Flyway Desktop execution from CLI and integrate into my
Sway + Wofi desktop environment.
Basically, there is what you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get an &lt;a href=&#34;https://simpleicons.org/?q=flayway&#34;&gt;Flyway icon&lt;/a&gt; and paste it into &lt;code&gt;flyway.svg&lt;/code&gt; file&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Copy that SVG file into
&lt;code&gt;$HOME/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/flyway.svg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Change the color for the icon by adding &lt;code&gt;fill=&amp;quot;#CC0200&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; to the path&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create an &lt;code&gt;$HOME/.local/share/applications/flyway.desktop&lt;/code&gt; file with the
content like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-toml&#34; data-lang=&#34;toml&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Desktop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;mf&#34;&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Application&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Flyway&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;GenericName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Database&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;migration&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;tool&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Database&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Migrations&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Made&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Easy&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Categories&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;IDE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Development&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Keywords&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Database&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;SQL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;IDE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;JDBC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;ODBC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;MySQL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Oracle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;DB2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;MariaDB&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Exec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;HOME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;local&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;share&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;flyway&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;flyway-desktop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;flyway-desktop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;--enable-features&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;UseOzonePlatform&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;--ozone-platform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;wayland&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;--no-sandbox&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;flyway&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;Terminal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kc&#34;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;MimeType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;application&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nx&#34;&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Because Flyway Desktop is Electron app, we are passing few flags to run it on
Wayland system. If you still use Xorg, then just remove those flags.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How to Setup and Host Personal Blog for free with GitHub and Hugo</title>
      <link>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-setup-and-host-personal-blog/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 13 Jul 2024 23:49:42 +0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-setup-and-host-personal-blog/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;So&amp;hellip; you are thinking about your own blog for a long time. But&amp;hellip; it all felt
complicated, required too much time and you were even not sure, what would you
write there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I can&amp;rsquo;t help you with the &amp;ldquo;what to write&amp;rdquo; part&amp;hellip; but, I can help to share my
experience about setting this blog up and hosting it for free.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I will try my best to write it a newbie friendly as I can, but it might be
challenging a bit as my own system and workflow is highly customized and I might
forgot that I have one or the other thing configured to make it work. And thus,
I migh write the workflow which does not work for you. If that is the case,
please feel free to ask for clarification in the GitHub issues. Just press the
&amp;ldquo;Suggest Changes&amp;rdquo; at the top of this article and open an
&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/dzintars/dzintars/issues&#34;&gt;Issue&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How to Store Ansible Vault Password</title>
      <link>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-store-ansible-vault-password/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 27 Mar 2024 13:18:12 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-store-ansible-vault-password/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;



&lt;img class=&#34;badge&#34;
	src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/Ansible-EE0000?logo=ansible&amp;logoColor=FFF&amp;style=flat&#34;
	alt=&#34;Ansible Badge&#34; /&gt;





&lt;img class=&#34;badge&#34;
	src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/KeePassXC-6CAC4D?logo=keepassxc&amp;logoColor=FFF&amp;style=flat&#34;
	alt=&#34;KeePassXC Badge&#34; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are several ways to pass the Ansible Vault password.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;classic CLI prompt which requires manual intervention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;password file which should be stored somewhere accessible to the Ansible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;environment variable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today I will tell about my latest approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am using tool called &lt;a href=&#34;https://direnv.net&#34;&gt;Direnv&lt;/a&gt; which loads and unloads different environment
variables when you enter the directory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direnv uses &lt;code&gt;.envrc&lt;/code&gt; files to read the variables from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typically, this file should be in your &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; so that you don&amp;rsquo;t leak any
secrets.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How to Integrate Google Analytics Into Hugo PaperMod Theme</title>
      <link>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-integrate-google-analytics-into-hugo-papermod-theme/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 22 Feb 2024 12:38:03 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:45463/posts/how-to-integrate-google-analytics-into-hugo-papermod-theme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As I&amp;rsquo;m setting up my shiny new blog, I stuck at Google Analytics integration.
It looks like official PaperMod lacks some documentation on this topic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So&amp;hellip; there is what worked for me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;rsquo;t use &lt;code&gt;analytics.google.SiteVerificationTag&lt;/code&gt; directive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use only &lt;code&gt;googleAnalytics: G-xxxxxxx&lt;/code&gt; directive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create new file in &lt;code&gt;layouts/_internal/google_analytics.html&lt;/code&gt; and paste the
entire code snippet you got from GA property setup page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Basically that&amp;rsquo;s it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This partial &lt;del&gt;will be&lt;/del&gt; should be automatically included in the every Hugo page.
And after your first visit to the page, you will see the first visitor stats on your GA
dashboard. If it doesn&amp;rsquo;t work immediately, then something is wrong. Might be
that Hugo upstream changed how it works. Check the &lt;a href=&#34;https://gohugo.io/templates/embedded/#google-analytics&#34;&gt;Hugo Docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
